    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0757" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg649"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Carter</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I receive with feelings of sincere sorrow
                    the intelligence of the death of His Majesty King Kalakaua, which you convey to
                    me in your note of this day’s date.</p>
                <p>The President, to whom I hastened to communicate the information, instructs me to
                    express through you his deep regret that Hawaii has lost a wise and good
                    sovereign, under whose beneficent rule the people of Hawaii have prospered, and
                    whose efforts have been so constantly and signally put forth to strengthen the
                    ties of mutual advantage between his Kingdom and the United States.</p>
                <p>The President further directs me to request you to convey to the royal family the
                    heartfelt sympathy he feels for their great affliction.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
